      <title>Poem of the week 10</title>
      <link>https://lightpoetrymagazine.com/poem-of-the-week-10/?utm_source=rss&amp;utm_medium=rss&amp;utm_campaign=poem-of-the-week-10</link>
      <description>Emily Dickinson Crushes on Edward Snowden I love—his pasty Skin— His Glasses—Intellectual— And most of all—his Lips—that blew— A Whistle—Ineffectual— If Amherst—were in Russia— Then He—were here with Me— We two Recluses—snowed in— A wintry Privacy— —Amit Majmudar</description>
